IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- United States Naval Communication Station (Civilian Employees) Act 1968
-- (Cth). Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C1968A00054.txt. Seat: the
-- civilian employee (or dependant).

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `Station worker` HAS
    -- s 4, 3(2)
    `employed by the US Government at the Station`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `a member of the US forces`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `a US citizen or national`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `on terms agreed with an Australian union`          IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 6
    `sections 9 or 10 of the compensation Act apply`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `damages recoverable had all been Commonwealth employees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury, disease or death on`                       IS A DATE

DECLARE `Station position` HAS
    `this Act applies to me`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the compensation Act applies to me`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `damages recoverable from the Commonwealth`         IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

@ref s 4
GIVEN w IS A `Station worker`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to` w IF
        w's `employed by the US Government at the Station`
    AND NOT (w's `a member of the US forces`)
    AND ((NOT (w's `a US citizen or national`)) OR w's `on terms agreed with an Australian union`)

-- s 6(1)-(2): after commencement, or from 29 August 1966.
@ref s 6(1)-(2)
GIVEN w IS A `Station worker`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `damages are recoverable for` w IF
        `the Act applies to` w
    AND w's `sections 9 or 10 of the compensation Act apply`
    AND w's `damages recoverable had all been Commonwealth employees`
    AND w's `injury, disease or death on` AT LEAST Date 29 8 1966

@ref ss 4-6
@export default The position of a civilian employee at the United States Naval Communication Station under the United States Naval Communication Station (Civilian Employees) Act 1968 (Cth): whether the Act applies (s 4), that the Commonwealth Employees' Compensation Act then applies as if they were an employee (s 5), and whether they (or another person on their death) may recover damages from the Commonwealth as if everyone at the Station had been employed by the Commonwealth (s 6), for injury, disease or death from 29 August 1966. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN w IS A `Station worker`  @desc The employment, citizenship and terms, and the injury facts
GIVETH A `Station position`
`the station position for` w MEANS
    `Station position` WITH
        `this Act applies to me`                        IS `the Act applies to` w
        `the compensation Act applies to me`            IS `the Act applies to` w
        `damages recoverable from the Commonwealth`     IS `damages are recoverable for` w
